-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",103,{
[3265]="7004E63E\n1\tTalk to Authi Gem-cutter in the Quenching Trough\tAuthi Gem-cutter is in the Quenching Trough.\n2\tTalk to Khîl in the Quenching Trough\tKhîl is in the Quenching Trough, quite distraught.\n3\tTalk to Khîl and travel to his father's home\tKhîl is in the Quenching Trough, quite distraught.\n4\tTalk to Náin in the hidden chamber\tNáin is in the hidden chamber in Khîl's home in Járnfast.\n",
[3266]="70059A1E\n1\tDefeat Angmarim cultists or Trév Duvárdain in Câr Bronach ([see journal]/8)\tVenko believes there is more to learn from the messages carried hither and yon by Angmarim cultists within Câr Bronach. He wants you to wrest from them any such missives.\n2\tDefeat Angmarim cultists or Trév Duvárdain in Câr Bronach (7/8)\tVenko believes there is more to learn from the messages carried hither and yon by Angmarim cultists within Câr Bronach. He wants you to wrest from them any such missives.\n3\tRead the orders from Magith\tYou retrieved a set of orders from one of the cultists you faced in Câr Bronach, and should read it to learn what you can of their movements and plans for the mountain passes.\n4\tBring the orders from Magith to Venko outside Tâg Fógarrach\tVenko is outside Tâg Fógarrach. No doubt the Zhélruka will be pleased to see the set of orders you recovered from the Angmarim cultist you defeated.\n5\tInvestigate the mountainside to the south-east, behind Tâg Fógarrach, and learn what could have shaken Venko's composure\tVenko saw something disturbing to the south-east, just behind Tâg Fógarrach, and he has asked you to investigate. Whatever he saw, the vision seems to have shaken the Zhélruka's composure.\n6\tSomeone watches\tVenko saw something disturbing by the mountainside to the south-east, behind Tâg Fógarrach, and he has asked you to investigate. Whatever he saw, the vision seems to have shaken the Zhélruka's composure.\n7\tTalk to Venko outside Tâg Fógarrach\tVenko is outside Tâg Fógarrach, disturbed by whatever it was he saw.\n8\tTalk to Imák south-west of Tûr Fúar\tImák is south-west of Tûr Fúar, stroking his beard thoughtfully.\n",
[3267]="70059A1F\n1\tTalk to Imák and sneak into the Drearspire of Tûr Fúar\tImák believes that the troubling presence that so disturbed Venko might be the result of a ritual being conducted by the Angmarim in Tûr Fúar, the Drearspire, and he wants you to investigate.\n2\tTalk to Venko north of the Witch-gate\tVenko is north of the Witch-gate.\n3\tReturn to the Witch-gate with Imák and Venko\tImák and Venko are prepared to depart Câr Bronach, and want to travel with you to the Witch-gate.\n4\tSomeone watches\tYou once again feel the watchful presence.\n5\tTalk to Imák at the Witch-gate\tImák stands at the Witch-gate, a haunted expression on his face.\n6\tTalk to Venko at the Witch-gate\tVenko is at the Witch-gate, waiting to speak with you about what you saw.\n",
[3268]="70047295\n1\tTalk to Bósi in the Hall under the Mountain\tBósi is in the Hall under the Mountain.\n2\tTalk to Bósi and go with him to see the king\tBósi has been instructed to bring you before the King under the Mountain.\n3\tTalk to King Thorin III at his throne in the Hall under the Mountain\tThorin III, King under the Mountain, is at his throne in Erebor.\n",
[3269]="700472B2\n1\tTalk to King Elessar in his throne room\tKing Elessar is in his throne room atop Minas Tirith.\n2\tTalk to King Elessar and attend the ceremony\tKing Elessar is in his throne room atop Minas Tirith.\n3\tTalk to King Elessar in his throne room\tKing Elessar is in his throne room atop Minas Tirith.\n",
[3270]="70025391\n1\tTalk to Radanir and travel with him to Zudrugund\tRadanir is at the camp-site of the Grey Company in the grove of trees to the east of Lhanuch. Radanir is waiting to speak with you, and together you will travel to Zudrugund with all haste to try and defend it from the uruks of which Ergothorn wrote. This quest is meant for a fellowship. If you choose to undertake this quest solo, you will receive an inspiration bonus, but the challenge will be great.\n2\tTalk to Corunir in Zudrugund\tCorunir is in Zudrugund. You have managed to stave off an attack on Zudrugund by the Grishgúk Uruks led by Núrzumgrat, and should speak now to Corunir.\n",
[3271]="7002161F\n1\tDefeat Ninkoth Berserker (total: 8)\030Defeat Ninkoth Despoiler (total: 6)\030Collect treasure coffers (total: 4)\tTreasure and Ninkoth uruks can be found throughout the ruins of Minas Elendúr and the Delotham under-cellars. Fúni Gem-cutter is waiting for you to retrieve as much treasure from the ruins as you can.\n2\tBring treasures to Fúni Gem-cutter in Minas Elendúr\tFúni Gem-cutter is in Minas Elendúr. You have done what Fúni asked, and should return to him with the treasures you have gathered.\n3\tTalk to Fúsi Gem-cutter at Echad Eregion\tFúsi Gem-cutter is at Echad Eregion. You have rescued his father and should bring the news to Fúsi.\n4\tTalk to Radanir at Echad Eregion\tRadanir is at Echad Eregion. The Rangers have been discussing something with Fúni Gem-cutter, now that he has been rescued, and Radanir may know more about it.\n",
[3272]="700147ED\n1\tSearch the Black Lake\030Search the top of the bottom portion of the Endless Stair\tThe Black Lake and the bottom of the Endless Stair are both among the Foundations of Stone. Lenglammel has asked you to search several locations for sign of either Mithrandir or the Elf Magor.\n2\tBring the burned hat to Lenglammel\tLenglammel is in her camp of Gwathrendath, among the Foundations of Stone. You have searched both locations, and found the burned hat of Gandalf in the middle of the Black Lake. The Endless Stair has been choked by burned and blackened rubble. It seems that Gandalf survived long enough to do battle with the Balrog, but what happened then is unknown to you. You should speak now to Lenglammel.\n",
[3273]="7002099B\n1\tTalk to Lothrandir at Sûri-kylä\tLothrandir is at Sûri-kylä, the major village of the Lossoth in Forochel. Calenglad has sent you to bring your message to Lothrandir, in Forochel, with the warning that he has lived among the Lossoth for so long that he may have taken on something of their customs and personalities.\n2\tTalk to Lothrandir and help him find the screaming shadow\tLothrandir is at Sûri-kylä, in Forochel. You have given Lothrandir the message, but he seems unsure of the Grey Company's ability to reach Aragorn in time and wants your help with a Lossoth issue.\n3\tTalk to Lothrandir at Sûri-kylä\tLothrandir is at Sûri-kylä, in Forochel. You have found the cause of the Lossoth's hunting troubles and have hopefully ended it. Lothrandir, at least, seems satisfied.\n",
[3274]="7001B77F\n1\tNervous Malledhrim can be found throughout Audaghaim. Issuriel has asked you to reassure nervous Malledhrim throughout Audaghaim that all will be well, despite the disturbing things they have seen at this abandoned village.\t\n2\tTalk to Issuriel at the Haunted Inn\tIssuriel is in the cellar of the Haunted Inn, in Audaghaim. You have reassured a number of nervous Malledhrim and should return to Issuriel.\n",
[3275]="7005A723\n1\tTalk to Prince Ingór\tVérnozal can be found in Máttugard, by the Steepset. Prince Ingór wishes to talk to you.\n2\tTalk to the Longbeard emissary at Vérnozal\tVérnozal can be found in Máttugard, by the Steepset. You should talk to the Longbeard emissary at Vérnozal.\n3\tTalk to Prince Ingór\tVérnozal can be found in Máttugard, by the Steepset. Prince Ingór wishes to talk to you.\n",
[3276]="70049F32\n1\tTalk to Orophin\tYou should talk to Orophin and join the War Council.\n2\tTalk to Galadriel\tTalk to Lady Galadriel to be released, finally, from your service.\n",
[3277]="70014647\n1\tTalk to Bori and travel to the Hall of Mithril\tBori is in the Chamber of Leadership off the Twenty-first Hall, in Zelem-melek. Bori is waiting to speak with you to travel to the Hall of Mithril, where he believes you will find the mithril axe Zigilburk. He asked you to bring allies. NOTE: It is suggested that you complete this quest while in a fellowship. Inspiration will assist you if you choose to undertake this challenge alone or with a smaller group.\n2\tTalk to Bori\tBori is in the Chamber of Leadership off the Twenty-first Hall, in Zelem-melek. You and Bori discovered Bróin, still alive despite great hardship, and brought him safely from the drowned treasury where he found the mithril axe Zigilburk.\n",
[3278]="70013AFD\n1\tTalk to Bósi and travel with him to find Nâr-khelab\tBósi is in the Chamber of the Cross-roads, near the southern entrance to Durin's Way, north of the Great Delving of Moria. Bósi believes he has intuited the hidden entrance to Nâr-khelab, the Heart of Fire, and is waiting to travel there with you.\n2\tTalk to Bósi\tBósi is in the Chamber of the Cross-roads, at the southern entrance to Durin's Way, north of the Great Delving of Moria. With Bósi's help, you discovered the hidden entrance to Nâr-khelab, the Heart of Fire, and should now speak with him.\n",
[3279]="7000F101\n1\tDefeat shadow-wargs (total: 3)\tShadow-wargs can be found south of the stairs that lead up to the pool in front of the Hollin Gate, on the other side of the Sirannon's dry river-bed. Bróin has somehow managed to foist his task off on you, and now you have to face the shadow-wargs in his stead.\n2\tTalk to Bróin\tBróin is at the base of the stairs that climb up to the foetid pool in front of the Hollin Gate, east of Bósi's location. You have defeated many shadow-wargs and should return now to Bróin.\n",
[3280]="70018F10\n1\tFind the workshop of Melkólf Stonecarver and search it for mention of Zurr-thurkh\tThe passage to Melkólf Stonecarver's workshop can be found in the side of Zirakzigil; take the western exit from the Peaceful Path, and then turn west and climb a short slope to the entrance. Bróin has asked you to find Melkólf Stonecarver's workshop and search it for any mention of Zurr-thurkh, the secret road into Durin's throne room that might have been built long ago. He has decided not to accompany you to the workshop.\n2\tTalk to Bróin\tBróin is in the Peaceful Path, located in the Mustering Hall, east of Sulnul-dûm and west of the Stone Hall, along Durin's Way. You have recovered a set of plans from Melkólf Stonecarver's workshop that reveal a secret way into Rushdurinul, the throne room of Durin, that is now occupied by Mazog and his Orcs.\n",
[3281]="700143DD\n1\tTalk to Bori and execute his daring plan to combat the White Hand\tBori is in the Chamber of Leadership off the Twenty-first Hall, in Zelem-melek. Bori is waiting for you to give the word, and he will then set his plan into motion.\n2\tTalk to Bori\tBori is in the Chamber of Leadership off the Twenty-first Hall, in Zelem-melek. Bori's plan has been successful, and you should now speak to him about it.\n3\tTalk to Brogur\tBrogur is in the Chamber of Leadership off the Twenty-first Hall, in Zelem-melek, with Bori. Bori is worried about Ashpar's final words, and wants you to ask Brogur for advice.\n",
[3282]="7000F100\n1\tFind the cause of the wolves' madness\030Help Bróin with the task Brogur gave him\tThe cause of the wolves' fearsome behaviour may be found among their lairs, south of Brogur's location and across the Sirannon's dry river-bed. Brogur believes the cave Filgogân may hold some clue to the wolves' madness, in the far south-western corner of the area. Bróin can be seen talking to Bori at the base of the stairs that climb to the pool in front of the Hollin Gate. Brogur has asked you to search for the cause of the shadow-wolves growing madness, and to help his son Bróin with a task. When you have done each of these things, he told you to speak with his cousin Bósi.\n2\tTalk to Bósi\tBósi is south of Brogur's location, in view of the stairs that lead up to the pool in front of the Hollin Gate. You have learned something of the Shadow-wargs' madness and aided Bróin with his task, and have been asked to speak now with Bósi.\n",
[3283]="70047B60\n1\tTalk to Pippin\tYou should talk to Pippin in Bâr Thorenion, and learn what sort of 'formal invitation' he and Merry are talking about.\n2\tTalk to Merry\030Talk to Pippin\tYou should talk to Pippin and Merry in Bâr Thorenion.\n",
[3284]="70059A6C\n1\tTalk to Venko and travel to Maergrind\tVenko is at the Witch-gate, waiting to speak with you before the three of you depart for Maergrind, the Noble Gate.\n2\tTalk to Durin at Maergrind, the Noble Gate\tDurin is at Maergrind, enraged by both Gorgar's attack and the words of the Orc leader.\n",
[3285]="7006983B\n1\tTalk to Nauriel outside the Harbour-warden's Tower\tNauriel stands outside the Harbour-warden's Tower.\n2\tTalk to Nauriel and help her pursue the fleeing members of the Kindred\tNauriel stands outside the Harbour-warden's Tower, preparing to pursue the escaping members of the Kindred deeper into the Citadel of Winds.\n3\tTalk to Nauriel outside the Harbour-warden's Tower\tNauriel stands outside the Harbour-warden's Tower.\n4\tTalk to Sigileth outside the Harbour-warden's Tower\tSigileth stands outside the Harbour-warden's Tower.\n",
[3286]="7004E650\n1\tTalk to Khîl in the hidden chamber\tKhîl Tale-spinner is in the hidden chamber in his father's house where you discovered the Black Book of Mordor.\n2\tPick up the Black Book of Mordor from the table where it lies\tThe Black Book of Mordor is on the table in the hidden chamber in Khîl's family home in Járnfast.\n3\tTalk to Durin in the hidden chamber\tDurin is in the hidden chamber in Khîl's family home in Járnfast.\n4\tDurin wanted to meet up on the road west of Utterby to admire his handiwork.\t\n5\tCatch up to the large party heading west\tDurin has spied a large party heading west on the road to the Lonely Mountain, and he wants to investigate.\n6\tTalk to Bótuz Frostblood among the large Zhélruka force\tBótuz Frostblood leads a group of Zhélruka toward the Dale-lands.\n7\tTalk to Durin among the large Zhélruka force\tDurin stands among the group of Zhélruka that intends to cross the Dale-lands.\n8\tHurry to King Thorin in the Hall Under the Mountain\tKing Thorin III is at his throne in the Hall Under the Mountain.\n9\tTalk to King Thorin in the Hall Under the Mountain\tKing Thorin III is at his throne in the Hall Under the Mountain.\n10\tTalk to Gandalf at his chambers in the Dwelling-halls and give him the Black Book of Mordor\tGandalf is at his chambers on the upper level of the Dwelling-halls of Erebor.\n",
[3287]="70059A6E\n1\tTalk to Búkk at Maergrind\tBúkk is at Maergrind. Durin asked you to collect salves and bandages from Búkk with which to heal the hurts of those dwarves who are not already beyond help.\n2\tLongbeards and Zhélruka were wounded during Gorgar's attack, and many of them require treatment for their wounds.\t\n3\tReturn the remaining supplies to Búkk at Maergrind\tBúkk is at Maergrind. You have treated the dwarves you could, and should now return the remaining supplies to Búkk.\n4\tTalk to Durin at Maergrind\tDurin is at Maergrind, furious at Gorgar's attack and grieving for the slain.\n5\tTalk to Slagvi at Maergrind\tSlagvi is at Maergrind.\n6\tTalk to Durin at Maergrind\tDurin is at Maergrind.\n7\tTalk to Slagvi at Maergrind\tSlagvi is at Maergrind.\n",
[3288]="70069869\n1\tMeet up with Sigileth and Corudan beside the road east of the Mâkhda Khorbo\tThe ruins of the Mâkhda Khorbo stand to the north-west of Umbar Baharbêl. Sigileth and Corudan asked to meet up with you there.\n2\tTalk to Corudan beside the road east of the Mâkhda Khorbo\tCorudan stands by the road east of the Mâkhda Khorbo, north-west of Umbar Baharbêl.\n3\tTalk to Sigileth beside the road east of the Mâkhda Khorbo\tSigileth stands by the road east of the Mâkhda Khorbo, north-west of Umbar Baharbêl.\n4\tCollect rusty weapons from outside the Mâkhda Khorbo (total: 4)\030Collect finger-bones from wights near the Mâkhda Khorbo (total: 4)\030Collect gemstones from spectres or darkwaters near the Mâkhda Khorbo (total: 3)\tSigileth asked you to retrieve a number of curious objects near the Mâkhda Khorbo so she may examine them.\n5\tBring the strange items she requested to Sigileth east of the Mâkhda Khorbo\tSigileth is waiting for you to return to her east of the Mâkhda Khorbo with the strange objects for which she asked.\n6\tTalk to Corudan by his sister east of the Mâkhda Khorbo\tCorudan is beside the road east of the Mâkhda Khorbo, north-west of Umbar Baharbêl.\n7\tTalk to Rukân down the hill to the east\tCorudan has asked you to speak with a distant onlooker down the hill to the east.\n8\tTalk to Sigileth beside the road east of the Mâkhda Khorbo\tSigileth is beside the road east of the Mâkhda Khorbo, north-west of Umbar Baharbêl.\n9\tTalk to Corudan beside the road east of the Mâkhda Khorbo\tCorudan stands by the road east of the Mâkhda Khorbo, north-west of Umbar Baharbêl.\n",
[3289]="7004E651\n1\tReturn to King Thorin with Gandalf's warning about the Zhélruka\tKing Thorin is at his throne in the Hall Under the Mountain.\n2\tTalk to King Thorin in the Hall Under the Mountain\tKing Thorin is at his throne in the Hall Under the Mountain.\n3\tFind Durin on the road that climbs into the Grey Mountains\tDurin has followed the Zhélruka into the Grey Mountains, and at King Thorin's request you should look for him on the road that climbs into Ered Mithrin.\n4\tTalk to Durin on the road that climbs into the Grey Mountains\tYou have found Durin on the road that climbs into the Grey Mountains.\n",
[3290]="7004E653\n1\tDefeat enemies in the Wyrmgap (total: 8)\030Travel with Durin to the Anvil on the Withered Heath\tDurin asked you to defeat enemies in the Wyrmgap on your way to the Anvil on the Withered Heath.\n2\tTalk to Durin by the Anvil on the Withered Heath\tDurin stands by the Anvil on the Withered Heath.\n3\tCollect drake-teeth on the Withered Heath (total: 3)\030Collect worm-hides throughout Ered Mithrin (total: 6)\tDurin has asked you to defeat some of the worms and drakes that stalk the Withered Heath and Ered Mithrin, and collect their teeth and hides.\n4\tTalk to Durin by the Anvil on the Withered Heath\tDurin stands by the Anvil on the Withered Heath.\n5\tCollect hatchling-wings in Ered Mithrin (total: 4)\030Collect burning scales in Ered Mithrin (total: 4)\030Travel with Durin to the canyons south of Stormwall\tDurin asked you to defeat enemies in the Vales of Mithrin.\n6\tTalk to Durin in the canyons south of Stormwall\tDurin is in the canyons south of Stormwall.\n7\tTravel to the old fortress of Skarháld, where the Zhélruka planned to encamp\tThe old fortress of Skarháld is south and west of the path to Stormwall.\n8\tTalk to Durin at the eastern entrance of Skarháld\tThe old fortress of Skarháld is south and west of the path to Stormwall. Durin is at the eastern entrance of the city, waiting to speak with you.\n",
[3291]="70059A6F\n1\tMeet up with Slagvi at the entrance to Gloomingtarn from Deepscrave\tSlagvi asked to meet with you at the entrance to Gloomingtarn from Deepscrave, where he fears the rune-stones warding passage to that sacred cavern may be threatened.\n2\tTalk to Slagvi at the entrance to Gloomingtarn\tSlagvi stands beside the rune-stone wards at the entrance to Gloomingtarn.\n3\tStudying the stones on either side of the entrance may reveal what happened to the wards that once blocked passage to Gloomingtarn.\t\n4\tTalk to Slagvi at the entrance to Gloomingtarn\tSlagvi stands at the entrance to Gloomingtarn, beside the broken wards.\n5\tDefeat Angmarim cultists within Gloomingtarn (total: 10)\tSlagvi asked you to defeat any Angmarim cultists you find lurking within the cavern of Gloomingtarn.\n6\tTalk to Slagvi by the lakeshore\tSlagvi stands beside the lakeshore in the vast cavern, deep in thought.\n7\tLook toward the island that stands in the lake\tSlagvi has asked you to look toward the Stone of Wakening, the island that stands in the lake.\n8\tTalk to Slagvi beside the lake in Gloomingtarn\tSlagvi stands beside the lakeshore in the vast cavern, deep in thought.\n9\tCross to the island and find the White Stone Forge and the Black Stone Anvil\tThe Wakening Stone stands in the middle of the lake in Gloomingtarn.\n10\tExamine the White Stone Forge on the island in the lake\tIt is said that Durin himself constructed the White Stone Forge and the Black Stone Anvil in the days after he first awoke.\n11\tTalk to Slagvi on the Stone of Wakening\tSlagvi has come to the Stone of Wakening, and he is not happy.\n",
[3292]="7006987D\n1\tCorudan has asked you to speak with residents of the Upper Ward of Umbar Baharbêl about Azagath and the other leaders of the Kindred that fled with him.\t\n2\tCorudan has asked you to speak with residents of the Lower Ward of Umbar Baharbêl about Azagath and the other leaders of the Kindred that fled with him.\t\n3\tGather information from residents in the Lower Ward (2/3)\tCorudan has asked you to speak with residents of the Lower Ward of Umbar Baharbêl about Azagath and the other leaders of the Kindred that fled with him.\n4\tFind the man wearing blue and silver on one of the north-south piers of the the Sail-haven\tA man in the Lower Ward told you he saw a well-dressed man in blue and silver walking along one of the north-south piers extending out into the waters of the Sail-haven, north-west of the Lower Ward.\n5\tTalk to Belondor in the Sail-haven\tBelondor stands atop one of the piers extending out into the waters of the Sail-haven.\n",
[3293]="70059A70\n1\tDefeat Angmarim in Gloomingtarn ([see journal]/101)\tSlagvi has demanded that you slay one hundred and one Angmarim as payment for their theft of the Black Stone Anvil.\n2\tDefeat Angmarim in Gloomingtarn (6/101)\tSlagvi has demanded that you slay one hundred and one Angmarim as payment for their theft of the Black Stone Anvil.\n3\tTalk to Slagvi on the island in the lake\tSlagvi is standing on the Stone of Wakening, the island in the middle of the Gloomingtarn lake.\n4\tMeet up with Bósi and the other Longbeards on the lakeshore\tBósi and some other Longbeards have come to the lakeshore in Gloomingtarn.\n5\tTalk to Bósi on the lakeshore in Gloomingtarn\tBósi is on the lakeshore in Gloomingtarn.\n",
[3294]="7006987F\n1\tTalk to Sirgon outside the Harbour-warden's Tower, in the Sail-haven\tSirgon stands outside the Harbour-warden's Tower, in the Sail-haven.\n2\tTalk to Sirgon outside the Harbour-warden's Tower and go with him to meet with Belondor\tSirgon stands outside the Harbour-warden's Tower, in the Sail-haven, waiting to go with you to meet with Belondor.\n3\tTalk to Hármelak inside her manor\tHármelak is inside her manor, waiting to speak with you about the Kindred of the Coins.\n",
[3295]="7004E654\n1\tTalk to Bótuz Frostblood at Skarháld\tBótuz Frostblood is near the top of the fortress of Skarháld.\n2\tFind Dóbrokh at the view from the high eastern arch\030Find Inek the Brash at the siege defences\030Find Kópat inside Tharrazhâr, the keep of Skarháld\030Talk to Dóbrokh\030Talk to Inek the Brash\030Talk to Kópat\tBótuz Frostblood told you to look for his chieftains Inek, Kópat, and Dóbrokh on the upper levels of Skarháld and in the keep.\n3\tTalk to Durin inside Tharrazhâr, the keep of Skarháld\tDurin is inside Tharrazhâr, the keep of Skarháld.\n4\tLeave the keep of Skarháld and learn what transpired outside\tYou heard raised voices outside the keep. What is happening?\n5\tTalk to Vútro the West-wind and learn how he was injured\tA crowd of dwarves surround a wounded Zhélruka warrior on the upper level of Skarháld.\n",
[3296]="70059A76\n1\tTalk to Bori on the lakeshore\tBori is on the lakeshore in Gloomingtarn.\n2\tTalk to Bróin on the lakeshore\tBróin is on the lakeshore in Gloomingtarn.\n3\tTalk to Fastrith on the lakeshore\tFastrith is on the lakeshore in Gloomingtarn.\n4\tTalk to Bori by the lakeshore and travel with him in search of the Black Stone Anvil\tBori is waiting by the lakeshore in Gloomingtarn for you to agree to his plan.\n5\tTalk to Bósi in Clovengap, north-east of the tunnel to Gloomingtarn\tBósi is in Clovengap, north-east of the tunnel to Gloomingtarn.\n",
})
